<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Copy for "Add a packaged food" (0.2, behind release.submitFood): two photos
  of a pack, the label read and checked, the food saved to the person's foods
  (and logged, when there is a meal) and sent to Opson's food database for
  review. A barcode miss, search, the + sheet and the Foods tab's Add a food
  open it. "Opson's food database" is said in plain words; there is no
  acronym. Nothing here states a nutrition number except the check lines,
  which only draw where the mode shows calories. Same rules as strings.xml:
  no backslash escapes, positional %1$s arguments.
-->
